\p
\v 21 And the \sc Lord\sc* \w God| strong="H430" \w* \w caused| strong="H5307" \w* \w a deep sleep| strong="H8639" \w* [to fall]{strong=“H5307” x-morph=“strongMorph: \sc Th\sc*8686”} \w upon Adam| strong="H121" \w*, [and he slept]{strong=“H3462” x-morph=“strongMorph: \sc Th\sc*8799”}: [and he took]{strong=“H3947” x-morph=“strongMorph: \sc Th\sc*8799”} \w one| strong="H259" \w* \w of his ribs| strong="H6763" \w*, [and closed up]{strong=“H5462” x-morph=“strongMorph: \sc Th\sc*8799”} \w the flesh| strong="H1320" \w* instead thereof; 
\v 22 \w And the rib| strong="H6763" \w*, which the \sc Lord\sc* \w God| strong="H430" \w* [had taken]{strong=“H3947” x-morph=“strongMorph: \sc Th\sc*8804”} \w from man| strong="H120" \w*, [made]{strong=“H1129” x-morph=“strongMorph: \sc Th\sc*8799”} \w he a woman| strong="H802" \w*, [and brought]{strong=“H935” x-morph=“strongMorph: \sc Th\sc*8686”} \w her unto the man| strong="H120" \w*.\f + \fr 2:22 \ft made: Heb. builded \f* 
