\v 36 \w And the Midianites| strong="H4092" \w* [sold]{strong=“H4376” x-morph=“strongMorph: \sc Th\sc*8804”} \w him into Egypt| strong="H4714" \w* \w unto Potiphar| strong="H6318" \w*, \w an officer| strong="H5631" \w* [of Pharaoh’s]{strong=“H6547”}, and \w captain| strong="H8269" \w* \w of the guard| strong="H2876" \w*.\f + \fr 37:36 \ft officer: Heb. eunuch: but the word doth signify not only eunuchs, but also chamberlains, courtiers, and officers \f* \f + \fr 37:36 \ft captain…: or, chief marshal: Heb. chief of the slaughter men, or executioners \f*
\c 38
\p 
\v 1 \w And it came to pass at that time| strong="H6256" \w*, \w that Judah| strong="H3063" \w* [went down]{strong=“H3381” x-morph=“strongMorph: \sc Th\sc*8799”} \w from his brethren| strong="H251" \w*, [and turned]{strong=“H5186” x-morph=“strongMorph: \sc Th\sc*8799”} \w in to a certain| strong="H376" \w* \w Adullamite| strong="H5726" \w*, \w whose name| strong="H8034" \w* was \w Hirah| strong="H2437" \w*. 
